				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1959,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Align Tauri invoke command names to snake_case convention\n\nThe Tauri commands `VineSubscribeNotifications` and `VineSubscriberCount` are registered on the Rust (Mountain) backend where the standard naming convention is snake_case. Wind's `tauri.invoke` and `Module.invoke` callers were using PascalCase, which would fail at runtime since the Tauri IPC dispatcher matches command names case-sensitively against the backend registration.\n\nRename both invoke targets in `Source/Effect/Vine/NotificationStream.ts` to match the Rust-side registrations: `vine_subscribe_notifications` and `vine_subscriber_count`. The error message strings are updated to match for consistency.\n\nNo behavioral changes — the commands themselves and their payload schemas are identical.",
			"SHA": "ec67e70c68f4b5e783af35224cb7945b4a09d16e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T15:41:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1959,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Wind): Remove unused ModelUpdateContent IPC channel route\n\nThe `model:updateContent` IPC route defined in Channel.ts is no longer consumed by any active IPC caller. The Model subsystem now handles content updates through a different path — likely via the per-subsystem tier routing or direct content synchronization effects rather than a named channel dispatch.\n\nRemove the route constant and its `// --- Model ---` section header from the channel catalog to keep the route registry clean and avoid confusion during debugging.",
			"SHA": "f2f0d2b1b79b88f2092d53d64a398b5dd40ad2cc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T15:09:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1959,
				11
			],
			"Message": "chore(Wind): Regenerate generated artifacts with upstream source corrections\n\nRe-run Wind/Codegen to refresh generated TypeScript files after upstream VS Code source changes:\n- CommandCatalog drops from 551 to 550 entries, removing the `\"editor\"` command registered in `chat/electron-browser/chat.contribution.ts:340` that was removed upstream\n- ServiceCatalog grows from 500 to 502 entries, adding IChatViewFactory and ISessionsPartService to replace two stale SSH remote agent host service files that were superseded upstream\n- ISessionsManagementService gains a `setActive(session: IActiveSession): void` method reflecting new upstream API surface\n- Per-service upstream files (IAgentFeedbackService, IAgentHostGitService, ISSHRemoteAgentHostMainService, ISSHRemoteAgentHostService, IViewDescriptorService) have their source line references corrected to match the current VS Code source positions\n\nNo runtime behavioral changes — only generated scaffolding refreshed for build-time structural verification.",
			"SHA": "e691ac64bec0dbd3a836263294baa94a00d1facf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T13:59:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1955,
				300
			],
			"Message": "chore(Wind): Regenerate service catalogs, upstream interfaces, and bridge shapes\n\nRe-run Wind/Codegen to produce the full set of generated artifacts for the 2026-05-26 cycle:\n- CommandCatalog (551 entries) and ServiceCatalog (500 entries) with updated version date\n- Per-service schema files under Effect/Generated/<DecoratorName>/<DecoratorName>Upstream.ts\n  for all ~500 service interfaces extracted from the VS Code source tree\n- 16 bridge shape Pick<> types for Workbench services (Activity, Clipboard, Command,\n  ContextKey, Dialog, Editor, Extension, Host, Keybinding, Lifecycle, Notification,\n  Product, Progress, Settings, Storage, Workspace)\n\nThe previous daily cycle's generated artifacts were removed in the prior commit and\nare now replaced with freshly-generated equivalents. All files carry the DO NOT EDIT\nBY HAND header and reference the upstream decorator source paths for build-time\nstructural verification.",
			"SHA": "14b52b87f178e4e1c53c1a41f579fee865e9af96"
		}
